WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.890
(pensive music)
(paper rolling)

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.260
- There's been a major
shift in the war in Ukraine.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.880
Kyiv has launched a counteroffensive

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.340
along the front lines to retake territory

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.520
and Russia has been getting
hit behind its own lines.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.430
In Moscow, there have been
multiple aerial drone attacks.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.130
In the border town of
Belgorod, violent incursions.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.740
In Crimea, an attack on an oil depot.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.440
And throughout Russia and
Russian-controlled territory,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.020
there have been strikes
on refineries, railways

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.480
and all kinds of other infrastructure.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.370
As Ukraine launches the counteroffensive

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.810
everyone's been talking about,

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.640
we mapped out some of the early signs

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.979
of its strategy and the
obstacles it has to overcome.

00:00:35.979 --> 00:00:38.850
(pensive music)

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.260
Let's start on the front lines.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.450
They stretch for some 600 miles

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.520
and experts say Ukraine
has begun to strike

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.640
in various places to probe for weaknesses.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.650
Ukraine has already had some success

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.510
with Ukrainian troops raising flags

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.460
as they liberate towns in the east.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.490
But Russia currently controls some 20%

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.310
of Ukraine's territory,
shaded in light red,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.600
and Ukraine will have to push

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.880
through the huge trenches, minefields

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.870
and ditches that Russia has
built to defend that territory.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.150
Adding to the challenges,
much of this land

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.500
is flat and open.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.730
That makes Ukraine's troops

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.650
and equipment vulnerable to strikes,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.480
especially since it
doesn't have the support

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.400
of aircraft to provide cover.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.230
Plus, the destruction of this dam

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.320
in Kherson flooded a key
part of the battlefield.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.270
Both sides blamed each other

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.820
but the destruction could
ultimately hurt Ukraine.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.280
Not only has the flooding forced thousands

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.780
of people from their homes,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.840
it makes it hard for Ukrainian
troops to cross this river,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.640
which ultimately makes it harder for them

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.760
to sever the land bridge
between Russia and Crimea.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.310
And it makes it easier
for Russia to move troops

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.830
and equipment to other
parts of the front lines.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.350
Now let's look at the
attacks inside Russia

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.090
and Russian-controlled territory.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.100
Hits on oil depots, railways

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.750
and other infrastructure are known

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.160
as shaping operations.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.570
They show how Ukraine is trying

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.160
to choke Russia's supplies off

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.484
while simultaneously
attacking the front lines.

00:01:59.484 --> 00:02:01.620
(rocket booming)

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.780
Ukraine staged similar attacks last year

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.230
using US-made HIMARS before
retaking key territory.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.450
Now it's armed with British
Storm Shadow missiles

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.800
that are fired from aircraft,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.530
which allow it to hit
targets even farther away.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.930
That could force Russia
to push supplies further

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.140
from the fighting and complicate
its delivery of food, fuel

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.970
and ammo to troops.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.160
In Belgorod, cross-border incursions

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.290
are forcing civilians to evacuate

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.870
and exposing gaps in Russia's defenses.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.800
They've been carried out

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.170
by Russian fighters who oppose the Kremlin

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.150
and have ties to Kyiv.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.550
That's led local officials
to call on Moscow

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.260
to send reinforcements.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.660
Moving soldiers away
from these front lines

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.070
and into Russian territory

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.200
could ultimately weaken Russia's defenses

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.260
and help Ukraine try to
take back some of its land.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.700
There have also been drone attacks

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.480
in Moscow over the Kremlin
and in wealthy suburbs.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.450
No one has been killed, but
with buildings cordoned off,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.240
windows shattered and drone
fragments in plain view,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.040
these attacks have
shattered the perception

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.960
in Russia that the conflict is playing out

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.760
in some far away land.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.280
Officials in Ukraine have
denied being behind them

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.870
but Russian president Vladimir
Putin has blamed Kyiv.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.787
(Vladimir speaking in Russian)

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.230
- [Shelby] These attacks
undermine Putin's narrative

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.570
that the so-called
special military operation

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.920
is going as planned

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.260
and they've also fueled internal divisions

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.360
with the head of the
Wagner paramilitary group

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.525
lashing out at Russian defense officials.

00:03:27.525 --> 00:03:31.358
(Yevgeny speaking in Russian)

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.500
- So how are these attacks
being viewed outside

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.790
of Russia and Ukraine?

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.490
So far, Western countries
like the US have continued

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.680
to funnel aid to Kyiv,
and if Ukraine shows

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.810
that it can use that
equipment effectively,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.893
they could supply even more
powerful weapons down the road

00:03:48.893 --> 00:03:50.550
(tank rumbling)

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.680
but they don't want a broader conflict.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.340
- We have been very clear
with the Ukrainians privately,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.350
we've certainly been clear publicly

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.620
that we do not support
attacks inside Russia.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.960
- And there's another
important country watching all

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.130
of this closely.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.240
China has signaled

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.640
that it does not want
to see Russia collapse

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.460
and Presidents Xi and Putin remain close.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.180
So if it looks like Russia
can't stand on its own two feet,

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.610
experts say Beijing could
potentially be moved

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.500
to send lethal aid to Moscow,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.630
which would mark a major
new phase of the war.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.380
(dramatic music)

